    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d158">

                <pb facs="0281" n="205" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg205"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.60d31/127½</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Mr. Landreth M. Harrison of the Division
                        of Eastern European A fairs</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-12-17">December 17, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Our counter-proposals were made known to the Minister of Finland on December 12,
                        1935.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d158-f1"/> The Minister, after studying the
                    working draft of the counter-proposals, sent Dr. von Numers, Secretary of the
                    Legation, to the Division of Eastern European Affairs to arrange with me <pb
                        facs="0282" n="206" xml:id="pg206"/> a cable to the Finnish Foreign Office
                    setting forth our counter-proposals with respect to Schedules I and II. Such a
                    cable was drafted and sent on December 13. The Minister was then furnished with
                    three copies of the attached schedules.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d158-f2"/> Two
                    copies were to be sent immediately by mail to Finland and the third to be
                    retained in the Legation’s files. The Minister stated that he should shortly
                    receive from Helsingfors his Government’s reaction to the counter-proposals.</p>
                <closer><signed>L. M. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
